// WP-C7.9 Packet A sentinel — signed `MIN / -1` traps with the OVERFLOW identity.
//
// NUM-INT-DIV-001: dividing the minimum signed value by `-1`, and taking its remainder by `-1`,
// trap "because the intermediate quotient is not representable". That is an overflow, not a
// division by zero, even though the operator is `/`.
//
// The LIKELY WRONG implementation this sentinel fails:
// one static trap category per operator, so `/` reports `DivideByZero` for every
// failure it has — including this one, whose divisor is `-1`.
//
// The minimum is built as `-MAX - 1` because it is not writable as a literal at any width — which
// is why this pair had no maintained coverage before Packet A.
fn main() {
    let base: Int16 = -32767i16;
    let min: Int16 = base - 1i16;
    println(min / -1i16);
}
